{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin and xamarin.forms xamarin and xamarin.forms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","fileName":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin and xamarin.forms xamarin and xamarin.forms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","fileName":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms","heading":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Xamarin enabled .NET applications to target iOS and Android with C# while calling each platform's native capabilities. Xamarin.Forms added a shared abstraction for common interface controls so substantial UI and application logic could be reused across mobile platforms.\n\nShared code does not erase platform differences. A cross-platform project still needs platform-specific startup, packaging, permissions, and integrations, with abstractions placed where behavior must diverge.\n\nThe emotion-detector project uses Xamarin.Forms as a small shared UI layer and a platform plugin for native camera access. Shared calls remain uniform, while Android and iOS packages provide separate implementations for behavior that cannot be cross-compiled directly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin and xamarin.forms xamarin and xamarin.forms","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","fileName":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin and Xamarin.Forms","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}